                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/siainbuletin/dotfiles/git/commits/c0b433ee31df6c9aa090e1c4d78aebe309dc4020",
                "verification": {
                    "payload": "tree 1908edbba71059ca6a5c29ec51c5a4b3f3978705\nparent 6628e1ca6eb2390e675667b239bd93b1536b175e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1794434238 +0200\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1794434238 +0200\n\n🐛 fix: DT Open PDF falls back to the previous PDF viewer and can log why a lookup fails\n\nThe fallback was hard-coded to Preview, so installing the app replaced the\nviewer the user had (Highlights). Now, with DT_OPEN_FALLBACK unset, the app\nopens non-DEVONthink PDFs with the viewer recorded by dt-open-install before\nit became the default (open -b), then Preview. DT_OPEN_FALLBACK=Highlights\nsets it explicitly.\n\nA failed lookup silently fell back, which hid the reason every PDF opened in\nthe fallback viewer. Adds DT_OPEN_DEBUG=1 (log in ~/Library/Logs), an alert\nfor the Automation-permission error (-1743), a guard for a non-list result,\nand a troubleshooting section in README.org with a Terminal test of the\nlookup. The tangled files are regenerated with the blank-line trimming that\nEmacs does. Also adds the comments to .stow-local-ignore from README.org.\nNot run on a Mac.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBSPryU16ZirHGRiaX\n",
